<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9085" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">col-lĭquesco</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conl-</span></b> ), lĭqui,
			ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i>, <i>to become
			fluid</i>, <i>to liquefy</i>, <i>melt</i>, <i>dissolve</i> (rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: cum aurum colliquisset, Varr.
			ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 334, 27 sq.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum aes colliquisset,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i>
			 (but Neue, Formenl. 2, 486, would read collicuisset in both
			these passages): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in pice colliquescere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 22, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">igni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 306, 10</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>:  lacrimis, <i>to melt into tears</i>, <i><span class="en">Fronto, Nep. Am. 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
